"""More of the engine's sentences as frames, for `wording`: the names and lines that are not finding titles, fixes or notes.

Each row is (key, the engine's English with holes). The Turkish is under the same key in
locales/findings/tr.json (`label_patterns`, `line_patterns`, `term_patterns`); a fixed sentence has no row here, only
its English text and translation in the JSON file (`labels`, `lines`, `terms`). The hole forms are described at the
top of wording.py. A plain hole holds only what is shown unchanged (a number, an address, a name, quoted site text);
a hole that holds English words is a "~" hole, so a sentence is never shown half translated.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

